  // Qwen-Drive-1.0 - the whole study, one keypress at a time.  F5 -> pick one.
  //
  // START HERE:  1a  (how 3D perception actually works, printed from a live forward)
  //              then read study/06_HOW_3D_PERCEPTION_WORKS.md alongside it.
  //              1a1 / 1a2 / 1a3 draw the figures that go with it.
  //
  // Every config sets "stopOnEntry": true, so the debugger breaks on the first line and
  // you can step from the top. Press F5 again (Continue) to just run it.
  // "justMyCode": true keeps stepping inside this repo and out of torch/transformers.
  //
  // GPU by default: the scripts default to --device cuda and --dtype bfloat16, so no
  // device flags appear here. Group 4 needs no GPU.
  //
  // GPU configs set CUDA_HOME and prefix PATH with .venv/bin, because torch shells out to
  // `ninja` to JIT-build the two perception CUDA kernels and the venv bin is not on PATH
  // when python is launched by absolute path.
  //
  // Plain ASCII on purpose - unicode escapes in this file break VS Code's config resolution.
